# zlib1g / MiniZip: Debian does not build MiniZip into zlib1g, so the vulnerable
# code is not present. Still relevant -- several repackaging/images.yaml entries
# pull external Debian-based images.
# Refs: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-45853
#       https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-45853
CVE-2023-45853

# setuptools 70.3.0 -- FALSE POSITIVE in base-python / stdio-wrapper.
# Trivy infers setuptools from pip's vendored manifest
# (site-packages/pip/_vendor/vendor.txt and bom.cdx.json), but pip only vendors
# pkg_resources. Verified in the built image: there is no pip/_vendor/setuptools
# directory and no package_index module, so the vulnerable code paths are absent.
# Re-check if pip ever starts vendoring setuptools proper.
CVE-2025-47273
CVE-2026-59890
